pocock-core
===========

The skills under `skills/` are vendored — copied, and in places modified — from:

    https://github.com/mattpocock/skills
    Copyright (c) 2026 Matt Pocock
    MIT License (see LICENSE in this directory)

They are NOT maintained by Matt Pocock in this form. Bugs you hit here may be
ours, not his. The upstream project is the canonical source; if you want the
complete, always-current set as the author ships it, install his plugin instead:

    /plugin install mattpocock-skills

(It is in Claude Code's official marketplace. Installing both gives you every
skill twice, so pick one.)

Which skills are vendored, from which upstream paths, and at which commit is
recorded in `UPSTREAM.json`. To pull in upstream changes while keeping local
edits, run:

    scripts/vendor-sync.py --check     # see what moved upstream
    scripts/vendor-sync.py             # 3-way merge it in

Eight skills were chosen deliberately:

    grill-with-docs, to-spec, to-tickets, triage,
    teach, writing-great-skills, research, wayfinder

Three more are vendored because the eight do not work without them:

    grilling                  grill-with-docs runs a /grilling session
    domain-modeling           grill-with-docs uses the /domain-modeling skill
    setup-matt-pocock-skills  to-spec, to-tickets, triage and wayfinder all
                              require the issue-tracker and triage-label
                              configuration it writes

Run `/setup-matt-pocock-skills` once per repository before using the others.
